<title>USA: U.S. CASH SOYMEAL - BASIS OFFERS STEADY-WEAK.</title>
<headline>U.S. CASH SOYMEAL - BASIS OFFERS STEADY-WEAK.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis offers for soymeal in truck and rail markets were steady to slightly weaker Tuesday as supply continued to outstrip demand,</p>
<p>&quot;I think there is meal available and business is rather slow,&quot; a Minnesota-based dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers said buyers were operating &quot;hand-to-mouth&quot; due to the large and widening August premium to September.</p>
<p>Some dealers reported signs that basis levels may, however, be starting to stabilise after their recent tumble. Basis levels at Illinois locations remain around $6.00 per ton down from a week ago.  </p>
